here not do this,

00:18:53.790 --> 00:18:57.570
but so I've got-- what I
do is I maintain-- everyone

00:18:57.570 --> 00:19:00.330
is special in case anyone
watches this video.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:01.260
Everyone's special.

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:03.630
But in order to
achieve scalability,

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:05.740
I do have to standardize
things a bit.

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:08.010
So I have on--

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:09.150
because we use Confluence.

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:11.400
So on the wiki that I've
made, I have a lockdown page

00:19:11.400 --> 00:19:13.950
where I have some
standardized messages

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:17.130
that I send out to people at
different phases of things.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:18.612
And I do customize
and I read what

00:19:18.612 --> 00:19:20.320
people say about
themselves and I'm like,

00:19:20.320 --> 00:19:22.870
OK, this could be useful here,
that could be useful there.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:26.130
So one of the things
that I do is--

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:29.130
I kind of have this
whole ingestion pipeline

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:33.210
that I maintain to identify
new members of the community,

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:36.960
and then of those members, who
can help the community learn

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:40.770
more about what the blockers are
to the current responsibilities

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:41.830
they have for their job.

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:44.610
So I mean, all companies
have a directory

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:48.630
where you can learn about
who exists at the company.

00:19:48.630 --> 00:19:50.650
You can see people's
job titles and stuff.

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:52.440
So one of the
things that I do is

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:54.180
I can look into
the directory and I

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:58.020
can look for like data or
data science or whatever.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:04.290
And then the people that
come out in the results

00:20:04.290 --> 00:20:05.820
like when I search
for those terms,

00:20:05.820 --> 00:20:09.480
I look to see if they're already
in my Microsoft Teams group.

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.040
And because I'm
thinking that they

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:13.100
could be potential
new people who

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:14.850
could benefit from
being in the community,

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.065
they might be able to do
their job better and also

00:20:17.065 --> 00:20:19.440
help other people do their
job better if they can connect

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:24.220
to others who have similar needs
or can offer similar things.

00:20:24.220 --> 00:20:26.430
So I look in the
company directory,

00:20:26.430 --> 00:20:28.990
and then-- and I do it
on a semi-regular basis,

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:32.233
so I can really help to
onboard people who have just

00:20:32.233 --> 00:20:34.650
joined the company or maybe
moved into a data science type

00:20:34.650 --> 00:20:35.200
role.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.900
So then I reach out
to these people,

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:39.170
and I use my standardized
thing like, hey,

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:40.920
I just want you to
know this group exists.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.003
And I only send one email.

00:20:42.003 --> 00:20:42.900
I don't spam people.

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:46.290
And I say like, hey, this
community was built just

00:20:46.290 --> 00:20:48.270
for people like you.

00:20:48.270 --> 00:20:49.225
This is what we do.

00:20:49.225 --> 00:20:51.600
Here's a link to the wiki that
has the lengths of all the

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:53.725
recorded-- because we have
a growing library of all

00:20:53.725 --> 00:20:56.010
the conversations just like
the Data Science Hangouts

00:20:56.010 --> 00:20:56.860
that you have here.

00:20:56.860 --> 00:20:59.490
So I send that link out to them.

00:20:59.490 --> 00:21:01.227
And I say, hey,
this is something

00:21:01.227 --> 00:21:02.310
that may be of use to you.

00:21:02.310 --> 00:21:03.510
Let me know if you're
interested in it.

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:04.175
I can add you.

00:21:04.175 --> 00:21:05.550
And look at all
the conversations

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:07.028
we've already had.

00:21:07.028 --> 00:21:08.820
You be able to already
do something with it

00:21:08.820 --> 00:21:10.420
yourself already.

00:21:10.420 --> 00:21:12.690
So then-- of the subset.

00:21:12.690 --> 00:21:13.830
Because it's not 100%.

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:16.590
Sometimes it's like
20% that respond.

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:18.280
And they say, yes,
this is amazing.

00:21:18.280 --> 00:21:19.020
Thank you for letting me know.

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.145
I just came to the company.

00:21:20.145 --> 00:21:22.210
I didn't even know if
there was a community.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.690
And I'm also doing it
from my own perspective

00:21:24.690 --> 00:21:25.420
of when I joined.

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:30.440
It was hard to see who
else may be able to speak

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:31.440
the same language about.

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:33.720
And not the language where
when you talk to someone,

00:21:33.720 --> 00:21:34.950
their eyes glaze over.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:37.050
It's not for the
non-computational.

00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:38.560
It's for the
computational people.

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:41.860
So when they respond
and then they say,

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:44.110
yes, they're interested,
then I add them to the group.

00:21:44.110 --> 00:21:46.950
But I have another thing
in my wiki for myself

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:50.850
in my lockdown page that is
the intro, the welcome words.

00:21:50.850 --> 00:21:54.660
So I add them to
the Teams group.

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:59.340
Then I add them to the Active
Directory group, the Listserv.

00:21:59.340 --> 00:22:03.120
And then I also
forward the invitation

00:22:03.120 --> 00:22:06.910
to the ongoing gatherings
so every other Friday.

00:22:06.910 --> 00:22:10.740
And in the invitation text I
paste in, welcome to the group.

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:12.990
Please introduce yourself
in the introduction section.

00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:16.695
And I include a link, which I
use a tiny URL for because I

00:22:16.695 --> 00:22:18.418
was using the full
URL from Confluence

00:22:18.418 --> 00:22:19.710
and it was chopping things off.

00:22:19.710 --> 00:22:22.240
But now that I use a tiny
URL, when they click it,

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:26.400
it takes them directly into not
just the Team for the group,

00:22:26.400 --> 00:22:28.140
but the channel
of introductions.

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:30.870
So since I switched
over, I've gotten a lot

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:33.510
higher percentage of people who
have been added to the group

00:22:33.510 --> 00:22:36.060
to start introducing themselves
and say what they work on.

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:38.130
So then I could see what
people are working on,

00:22:38.130 --> 00:22:40.980
and then I integrate that
with my understanding of what

00:22:40.980 --> 00:22:42.780
the output is, what
people have voted on

00:22:42.780 --> 00:22:44.550
that they need help with
from the Shiny app that's

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:46.110
the poll for what people
are interested in.

00:22:46.110 --> 00:22:48.068
And that's an open ended
thing too, by the way.

00:22:48.068 --> 00:22:50.340
It's not that's
fixed set of things.

00:22:50.340 --> 00:22:52.830
In Shiny, you can configure
it so that you can actually

00:22:52.830 --> 00:22:53.610
add things in.

00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:54.960
And that's got a MySQL back end.

00:22:54.960 --> 00:22:57.510
So whatever people pick
from the dropdown menu,

00:22:57.510 --> 00:23:00.090
it stores everything
in the back end

00:23:00.090 --> 00:23:02.010
and then since I'm
using a global object--

00:23:02.010 --> 00:23:03.270
I'm all over the
place, I apologize.

00:23:03.270 --> 00:23:04.770
But since I'm using
a global object,

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:06.240
whenever anyone
updates something,

00:23:06.240 --> 00:23:07.830
it automatically updates
the global object

00:23:07.830 --> 00:23:08.997
and that propagates it down.

00:23:08.997 --> 00:23:11.640
So it updates everybody's plot
regardless of what computer

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:13.300
you're looking at.

00:23:13.300 --> 00:23:15.380
But I use that, and
then I integrate it

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:17.130
with what people say
in their introduction

00:23:17.130 --> 00:23:18.910
and then I reach out
to them and say, hey,

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:20.880
would you be
interested in being one

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:22.380
of the guess for
an upcoming thing?

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:23.400
And then I send them the link.

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:24.960
And they can see
