00:39:19.850 --> 00:39:25.820
and elevate more of those
examples of connecting people

00:39:25.820 --> 00:39:27.780
across an organization?

00:39:27.780 --> 00:39:32.610
So I mean, since
my memories begin,

00:39:32.610 --> 00:39:35.690
so I think six years
old or something,

00:39:35.690 --> 00:39:36.920
it's always been the case.

00:39:36.920 --> 00:39:38.870
And I'm glad that so
many people are still

00:39:38.870 --> 00:39:40.245
on the call and
paying attention.

00:39:40.245 --> 00:39:42.710
I'm always working
on editing and--

00:39:42.710 --> 00:39:46.310
but this is also our community,
so it's easier to understand.

00:39:46.310 --> 00:39:48.440
But since as long
as I can remember,

00:39:48.440 --> 00:39:51.080
I've been familiar
with people's eyes

00:39:51.080 --> 00:39:53.660
glazing over when
I explain things.

00:39:53.660 --> 00:39:55.700
And adults, people
like 10 times my age

00:39:55.700 --> 00:40:03.370
when I was a little kid all
the way up until now, that is--

00:40:03.370 --> 00:40:04.870
I don't think it's
going to go away.

00:40:04.870 --> 00:40:07.450
I mean, maybe if ChatGPT
becomes even better

00:40:07.450 --> 00:40:09.522
and then we become
obsolete, OK, maybe.

00:40:09.522 --> 00:40:10.980
But there's so many
different ways.

00:40:10.980 --> 00:40:13.800
I don't think that's
going to go away.

00:40:13.800 --> 00:40:19.650
I think the way to
prove the contribution,

00:40:19.650 --> 00:40:24.590
the benefit of a community is--

00:40:24.590 --> 00:40:28.100
I used the word stuck
and the other word

00:40:28.100 --> 00:40:31.912
unstuck because that's really
the only thing the business,

00:40:31.912 --> 00:40:33.620
any business, any
organization that's not

00:40:33.620 --> 00:40:35.090
even a business cares about.

00:40:35.090 --> 00:40:38.090
There's a bunch of stuff that
the organization has to do.

00:40:38.090 --> 00:40:40.790
There are obstacles in
the way, they are stuck.

00:40:40.790 --> 00:40:42.255
How do they get unstuck?

00:40:42.255 --> 00:40:43.880
That's all data
science is for, really.

00:40:43.880 --> 00:40:45.530
Well, you could probably
do it for exploration

00:40:45.530 --> 00:40:46.310
and a bunch of other stuff.

00:40:46.310 --> 00:40:47.977
But you can argue
that maybe that's also

00:40:47.977 --> 00:40:49.490
for going from stuck to unstuck.

00:40:49.490 --> 00:40:51.710
But the non-computational
people who

00:40:51.710 --> 00:40:56.780
have the power to bestow upon
you promotions and more money

00:40:56.780 --> 00:41:00.080
or whatever you value, more
influence over the company

00:41:00.080 --> 00:41:02.180
to make other
decisions, they really

00:41:02.180 --> 00:41:04.700
care about what is the
value of the institution.

00:41:04.700 --> 00:41:06.800
If it's a business,
business value, going from

00:41:06.800 --> 00:41:08.360
stuck to unstuck.

00:41:08.360 --> 00:41:11.720
If you can show to--

00:41:11.720 --> 00:41:14.040
I forgot who was asking the
thing earlier about a graph

00:41:14.040 --> 00:41:14.540
database.

00:41:14.540 --> 00:41:16.430
It doesn't necessarily
need to be instantiated

00:41:16.430 --> 00:41:17.280
in a graph database.

00:41:17.280 --> 00:41:20.900
But if you can show how the
existence of that community

00:41:20.900 --> 00:41:22.550
propagates through
the network that

00:41:22.550 --> 00:41:26.600
exists in the institution
to such an extent

00:41:26.600 --> 00:41:29.210
that something goes
from stuck to unstuck

00:41:29.210 --> 00:41:32.490
and you can mark that,
you can measure it,

00:41:32.490 --> 00:41:35.120
then you can say this only
happened because of me.

00:41:35.120 --> 00:41:38.060
I mean, there are other
types of organizations

00:41:38.060 --> 00:41:39.660
which also should exist too.

00:41:39.660 --> 00:41:42.230
But sometimes, they're
based on interest.

00:41:42.230 --> 00:41:45.650
But interest is a lot
more difficult to prove

00:41:45.650 --> 00:41:49.010
the benefit of than, for
lack of a better word,

00:41:49.010 --> 00:41:51.710
pain-focused groups.

00:41:51.710 --> 00:41:53.240
Like if you're a
community that's

00:41:53.240 --> 00:41:57.290
gathered around pulling thorns
out of your colleagues arms,

00:41:57.290 --> 00:42:00.110
then you can be like,
we pulled 15 thorns out

00:42:00.110 --> 00:42:04.280
or we taught another group
how to pull 100 thorns out

00:42:04.280 --> 00:42:07.220
because we were
forced multipliers.

00:42:07.220 --> 00:42:08.960
That, I think, is
the way to prove

00:42:08.960 --> 00:42:10.400
the impact of the community.

00:42:10.400 --> 00:42:11.930
I'm not 100% sure
it's going to work

00:42:11.930 --> 00:42:13.070
because they're still
going to be people

00:42:13.070 --> 00:42:14.360
with eyes getting glazed over.

00:42:14.360 --> 00:42:17.090
But if you say, what do
you hate about your job,

00:42:17.090 --> 00:42:18.530
you person with
power that I need

00:42:18.530 --> 00:42:21.530
to prove the use of
this community of to?

00:42:21.530 --> 00:42:24.530
And then if you understand that
or maybe don't even ask them,

00:42:24.530 --> 00:42:27.110
but you may know because they're
probably high enough profile

00:42:27.110 --> 00:42:29.693
people at your institution that
you know what their values are

00:42:29.693 --> 00:42:31.550
likely to be, if you
can think about how

00:42:31.550 --> 00:42:35.060
the efforts that you're doing
propagate to the reduction

00:42:35.060 --> 00:42:38.060
of pain points for those people
and enables them to go from

00:42:38.060 --> 00:42:41.060
stuck to unstuck, then
collect those things.

00:42:41.060 --> 00:42:43.400
And do like what I did
with the showcasing.

00:42:43.400 --> 00:42:46.280
You could show like, hey,
people in this organization

00:42:46.280 --> 00:42:49.460
did this, this,
this, and this, then

00:42:49.460 --> 00:42:53.235
I think that could be
a way to prove impact.

00:42:53.235 --> 00:42:55.480
Thank you for that.

